{"type":"text","timestamp":1794364063690,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c86ebfba001BmZIRu64MxpjKJ","messageID":"msg_1c86eb005001I1mONuOgnOepUq","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"text","text":"<think>Hmm, `_now` is defined in auth.py but I need it in db/app too. Better to put a shared `now_iso()` helper in db.py or a separate module. Let me create `backend/utils.py`? Or put `now_iso` in db.py and import from there. Actually let's put it in `db.py`... that's odd semantically. I'll create a small `backend/timeutil.py`... Simpler: put `now_iso()` in `db.py`? Hmm.\n\nCleanest: create `backend/helpers.py` with `now_iso()` and `clean_text()`? Actually text cleaning belongs in fetcher. Let me just add `now_iso()` to db.py — no. I'll make a tiny module `backend/clock.py`? Overkill.\n\nLet me put `now_iso()` in `auth.py`? It's used by app.py for previews too — app.py can import from auth. That's a bit odd but acceptable: `from auth import now_iso`. Let me rename `_now` to `now_iso` in auth.py and export it properly. Actually, better placement: `db.py` already deals with persistence and could host `now_iso` since it stores timestamps. Hmm, I'll create `backend/utils.py` with `now_iso()` and `to_plain_text()` maybe. Let me do utils.py — clean.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794364063674,"end":1794364063686}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794364063711,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c86ebb2674b1b48dfc41","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Small shared helpers.\"\"\"\n\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\n\ndef now_iso() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Current UTC time as an ISO-8601 string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"microseconds\").replace(\"+00:00\", \"Z\")\n","filePath":"/workspace/backend/utils.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/backend/utils.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"backend/utils.py","time":{"start":1794364063682,"end":1794364063692}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c86ebfbd001G36iEC09pumWQN","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","messageID":"msg_1c86eb005001I1mONuOgnOepUq"}}
