{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794364155187,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c870251c001bKP2O8QZxEQTsi","messageID":"msg_1c8700651001chTbHXxLCf1nz4","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794364155187,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c8702520001vdPnOBMVQd76Za","messageID":"msg_1c8700651001chTbHXxLCf1nz4","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"text","text":"<think>The lock was generated, but the \"# via\" comments reference the constraints file which is temporary. Let me clean that up — regenerate using a constraints file placed at a stable path, or just post-process the lock to remove \"-c /workspace/.tmp-constraints.txt\" lines.\n\nBetter: put the constraints file inside the repo temporarily as `backend/requirements.lock` generation input? Simplest: post-process with sed to drop the `-c ...` lines. But the \"via\" comments would then just say \"# via -r backend/requirements.txt\" for direct deps and for transitive deps just the parent. That's acceptable and matches pip-compile style.\n\nLet me look at the generated file and clean it up.\n\nAlso check the header of the generated file (pip-compile adds a header comment with the command). The original lock file starts directly with \"blinker==1.9.0\" — no header. Let me check what the new one looks like.\n\nAlso note pip-compile resolves only for the current Python/platform by default? With --generate-hashes it includes hashes for all available wheels (it uses --all-extras? no). pip-compile includes hashes for all files of the pinned version found on the index (it uses `pip download`-like resolution across platforms) — actually pip-compile generates hashes for all distributions matching the requirement across platforms. The original lock had many hashes per package (e.g. blinker had 2 = sdist + wheel). Let me check the new file has the same style.\n\nLet me read the generatedfile.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794364155168,"end":1794364155183}}}
