{"type":"text","timestamp":1794364260663,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c871c1230016KsJ86HuQTzcPZ","messageID":"msg_1c871b528001M19ddJgwTGaRbe","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"text","text":"<think>Writing to /tmp/opencode is blocked by the tool's external directory rules (the allow pattern for /tmp/opencode/* seems to apply to bash commands maybe). Let me instead put the smoke test inside the workspace at `backend/tests/smoke.py`? Or in a workspace-level `tests/` dir. Actually having a test in the repo is a plus for the deliverable. But careful: the Dockerfile copies `backend/` into the image; a test file there is harmless.\n\nI'll put it at /workspace/tests/smoke_test.py (workspace root, not copied into the image). Hmm, .dockerignore doesn't exclude tests/, but the Dockerfile only copies backend/ and frontend/dist, so it's not in the image. Good.\n\nLet me write it there.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794364260643,"end":1794364260659}}}
