{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794364294660,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c87245f2001DPoYJ0VeExIddD","messageID":"msg_1c87228f3001Eo1cZDVGufrIic","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794364294661,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"id":"prt_1c87245f500154GkWqKs0dAX10","messageID":"msg_1c87228f3001Eo1cZDVGufrIic","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","type":"text","text":"<think>Almost everything passes. The one real bug: \"not a url\" was accepted (201) because normalize_url prepends \"https://\" and urlparse(\"https://not a url\") gives netloc \"not a url\" — hmm, urlparse of \"https://not a url\" → netloc = \"not a url\" (with space). My check `parsed.netloc` is truthy → accepted. I should validate that the host doesn't contain spaces/invalid chars.\n\nLet me improve normalize_url: after parsing, validate the hostname matches a reasonable pattern (no spaces, no invalid characters). Use a regex for hostnames/IPv6.\n\nApproach:\n```python\nhost = parsed.hostname  # lowercased, strips brackets for ipv6\nif not host: return None\nif re.search(r\"\\s\", host): return None\n```\nAlso validate that the netloc has no spaces at all. And check the host is a valid domain or IP: `re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z0-9._\\-]+\", host)` or IPv6 (contains \":\").\n\nLet me write:\n\n```python\nHOST_RE = re.compile(r\"^(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\\.(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*\\.?$\")\n```\nThat's the classic hostname regex. Plus allow IPv4 (digits/dots, matches above) and IPv6 (contains \":\").\n\nSimplest robust check:\n```python\nhost = parsed.hostname or \"\"\nif not host or any(ch.isspace() for ch in parsed.netloc):\n    return None\nif \":\" not in host and not HOST_RE.match(host.lower()):\n    return None\n```\nAlso require a dot in the host? \"localhost\" is valid (no dot) and useful for local fixture servers! So don't require a dot.\n\nAlso \"not a url\" → after prefixing https:// → netloc \"not a url\" → contains space → rejected → 400.\n\nAlso, what about a URL like \"htp://foo\"? scheme not http/https → rejected.\n\nAlso \"http://\" → netloc empty → rejected.\n\nNow, the other failures were cascading from the extra preview (total 3 vs 4). After the fix, those pass.\n\nAlso note: the \"url\" for the invalid case — not stored now.\n\nLet me also double check the `url` stored for \"not a url\" won't be created anymore.\n\nOne more consideration on `normalize_url`: the `url` column stores the RAW url (as given). Good.\n\nLet me apply the fix.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794364294645,"end":1794364294657}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794364294690,"sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH8FUfoum56bQ5v","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c8724163756e88667c74","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/fetcher.py","newString":"VERIFY_SSL = os.environ.get(\"VERIFY_SSL\", \"1\").lower() not in {\"0\", \"false\", \"no\"}\n\nHOSTNAME_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"^(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\\.(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*\\.?$\"\n)","oldString":"VERIFY_SSL = os.environ.get(\"VERIFY_SSL\", \"1\").lower() not in {\"0\", \"false\", \"no\"}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n@@ -19,9 +19,13 @@\n MAX_DESCRIPTION = 4_096\n \n VERIFY_SSL = os.environ.get(\"VERIFY_SSL\", \"1\").lower() not in {\"0\", \"false\", \"no\"}\n \n+HOSTNAME_RE = re.compile(\n+    r\"^(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\\.(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*\\.?$\"\n+)\n \n+\n @dataclass\n class FetchResult:\n     \"\"\"Outcome of fetching a page.\"\"\"\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/backend/fetcher.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/fetcher.py\n@@ -19,9 +19,13 @@\n MAX_DESCRIPTION = 4_096\n \n VERIFY_SSL = os.environ.get(\"VERIFY_SSL\", \"1\").lower() not in {\"0\", \"false\", \"no\"}\n \n+HOSTNAME_RE = re.compile(\n+    r\"^(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-)(\\.(?!-)[a-z0-9-]{1,63}(?<!-))*\\.?$\"\n+)\n \n+\n @dataclass\n class FetchResult:\n     \"\"\"Outcome of fetching a page.\"\"\"\n \n","additions":4,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"backend/fetcher.py","time":{"start":1794364294653,"end":1794364294670}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c87245f7001jk3tXpSKI0CBtw","sessionID":"ses_e37936048ffeH